My structure is simple. Profit equals revenue minus cost, so I want to look both sides.

On revenue: is the growth coming from more stores, or more customers per store, or higher price? Because if we open many new stores, new stores maybe not yet profitable, and that alone can drag margin.

On cost: I want to split fixed and variable. Variable — coffee beans, milk, cups. Fixed — rent, labor if it is salary, marketing, corporate overhead.

Then I compare: which cost line grew faster than revenue over two years.

Can I start with the cost side? I think the answer is there, because revenue is still growing.
